:: Day5_SQ_Ali [day5 sidequest neighborhood ali]
<<nobr>>
<<centerImage "image/location/park.png">>

<p>"Alex! Come, come." Ali waves me in before I've even reached the door. The crossword is spread on the counter, pen in hand, reading glasses perched on his nose like they're trying to escape.</p>
<p>"Seven letters. 'A complete loss of identity.' Starts with E."</p>
<p>I think. My brain offers options like a multiple-choice test where all the answers are wrong.</p>
<p>"Eclipse?"</p>
<p>"Eclipse! Seven letters, E-C-L-I-P-S-E." He writes. Checks the crosses. "Perfect. Eclipse. When one thing covers another and the original disappears." He looks at me over his glasses. "Interesting word. An eclipse isn't destruction. The original is still there. It's just... hidden. Waiting for the shadow to pass."</p>
<p>He bags my Gatorade. Slides a chocolate bar in without charging. The Ali tax, free snacks for crossword assistance, a barter system as old as their relationship.</p>
<p>"You seem lighter today, Alex." He caps his pen. "Not lighter in weight. Lighter in... resistance. Like you stopped fighting the current."</p>
<p>"I didn't know I was fighting anything."</p>
<p>"Nobody does." He smiles. The smile of a man who solves crosswords and sees patterns in words that other people use without thinking. "That's what makes the current so effective."</p>

<<set $aliFamiliarity += 1>>
<<set $money -= 1>>
<<set $day5_aliCrossword to true>>
<<spendTime 1>>
<<set $currentMapLocation to "neighborhood">>

<<link "Continue" "DailyHub">><</link>>
<</nobr>>

:: Day5_SQ_Henderson [day5 sidequest neighborhood henderson]
<<nobr>>
<<centerImage "image/events/street.png">>

<p>Morning departure. Henderson is doing what Henderson always does, which is existing in his front yard like a man who was planted there by the neighborhood's original developer and has been growing ever since. Orioles cap. Garden hose. The same satisfied expression of someone who has figured out exactly what life is and decided it's watering the lawn.</p>
<p>"Morning, son!" He waves. The hose oscillates. Droplets catch the sun.</p>
<p>"Morning, Mr. Henderson."</p>
<<if $hairClipQuest>>
<p>"That your hair clip?" He points at the sparkly pink butterfly. Not accusatory. Not mocking. Just noticing. The way he'd notice a new mailbox or a different car in the driveway. Henderson notices everything and judges nothing.</p>
<p>"It's my sister's," I say. The lie is automatic. The truth would require an explanation that would take longer than Henderson's attention span, which is calibrated to lawn-sized increments.</p>
<p>"Huh. My wife used to wear butterflies in her hair." He adjusts his cap. "You look like your mother today. Something about the eyes."</p>
<<else>>
<p>He squints at me through the oscillating spray. "You look different today." Not accusatory. Not mocking. Just noticing. The way he'd notice a new mailbox or a different car in the driveway. Henderson notices everything and judges nothing.</p>
<p>"Do I?"</p>
<p>"Huh." He adjusts his cap. "You look like your mother today. Something about the eyes."</p>
<</if>>
<p>He means Evelyn. He's always called her my mother. To Henderson, step-parents are parents and the prefix is a technicality that doesn't survive contact with his worldview.</p>
<p>But he said I look like Evelyn. Not walk like her, which he said yesterday. Look like her. The observation has migrated from behavior to appearance. From motion to identity. Henderson is watching me become someone else in real time and reporting his findings with the detached accuracy of a nature documentary narrator.</p>
<p>"Must be the light," I say.</p>
<p>"Could be." He goes back to his hose. "Good light today. Makes everything look softer."</p>
<p>I walk to the bus stop. I think about looking soft. I think about Henderson, who has no agenda and no plan and no leverage, who just stands in his yard and says what he sees. And what he sees is a boy who looks like his stepmother<<if $hairClipQuest>> and wears butterflies in his hair<</if>> and walks smoother every day.</p>
<p>If Henderson can see it, everyone can see it.</p>

<<set $hendersonFamiliarity += 1>>
<<set $day5_hendersonMorning to true>>
<<spendTime 1>>
<<set $currentMapLocation to "neighborhood">>

